00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.070 align:start position:0%
 
there are brand new allegations against  tsm owner reginald of him being a  volatile ceo who created a toxic  workplace former tsm player doublelift  has spoken up to say that reginald  threatened to sue him for allegations he  publicly made last year it's the latest  chapter in a deepening controversy  here's all the details  all right there's a very good chance  that you're familiar with the previous  videos we've made on this subject but if  you're not here's a quick refresh  doublelift spent a number of years as  tsm's a.d carry on their league of  legends team helping them to multiple  lcs titles in november 2021 he was  involved in a public war of words with  tsm's owner reginald over the  circumstances of his departure from the  team the year before doublelift had said  that he wanted to keep playing for the  team especially with star support sword  art but that reginald refused because he  had quote too much of an ego reginald  hit back with a reddit post disputing  doublelift's account claiming that  doublelift was quote upset because we  weren't interested in working with him  and then the floodgates opened people  don't like working with them it's funny  that he has his holier than that  attitude about it because  he's like a bully who gets away with  being a bad person  because he's powerful because people are  afraid to stand up to him and that's  what i'm sick of so i would just say  that he made a lot of players cry you'd  be very [ __ ] surprised  at how many of maybe your favorite  familiar faces in lcs legit mental  breakdown because of how badly  they've been getting berated how badly  they were just getting verbally  assaulted this wasn't the first time  that accusations against reginald's  conduct have been made clips resurfaced  of old exchanges from the early days of  tsm between reginald and former players  that were used by people to back up  doublelift's claims  it feels like like you're just trying to  put it all in turtle no i'm not putting  it all into it no you are putting it on  turtle  okay  yeah  oh yeah you are yeah yeah  okay yeah i know that but so do you say  why are you arguing with me about it  it's so true though in january this year  wyatt published their investigation into  the matter including a statement from  riot that they were aware of the  allegations and had launched an  independent investigation into the  claims they also shared anonymous  accounts from former tsm staff claiming  they have been subjected to mental abuse  by reginald and that they've been  dominated by a culture of fear at tsm in  which he called them stupid or worthless  and called them after work at times to  scream at them tsm also announced they'd  be conducting their own internal  investigation  it's the findings of these two  investigations that the community has  been waiting on this week we didn't get  those findings but we did get something  else on wednesday the washington post  mikhail clementoff published an article  detailing the termination of a former  head of human resources for tsm weeks  after his hiring the hr head was  allegedly fired over a recruitment  practice he wanted to implement when an  employee asked reginald what prompted  the firing the source said quote that  was when andy told the whole company  that the hr person was let go because he  asked a question that andy didn't like i  think he kind of realized how ridiculous  it sounded so he followed up by saying  well he asked two questions that i  didn't like the article also quoted  anthony barnes a former senior program  manager at blitz the desktop gaming app  owned by tsm he said quote nobody wanted  to be in a one-on-one meeting with andy  because you had no witnesses i mean that  literally who knew if andy was going to  scream or yell at you degrade you be  friendly or just be confused or  inquisitive you weren't sure what andy  you were going to get but the more  people on the call the more likely andy  wasn't going to be a complete volcano  the report also detailed that multiple  workers at tsm and blitz have been  misclassified as contractors rather than  full-time employees this is a key  distinction under labour laws because it  dictates how workers are paid what  benefits they receive and what legal  rights they have a misclassification  could be a serious breach by any company  tsm told the washington post that they  would not be commenting on any  misclassification complaints the report  also shared stories of former tsm and  blitz employees experiences at their  companies these included allegations of  contractors being expected to work 40  hours a week and show up for work at 9  00 am all being paid below the legal  annual minimum for contract work in  california aside from that there was  also an account of reginald calling  individuals or teams out in public work  channels for work that he found is  satisfactory one former blitz employee  recounted that after tsm's ballarant  squad lost in 2020's first strike  tournament reginald joined work calls to  quote ream and tear down employees and  that they felt like they were quote  being hunted that day tsm reiterated two  comments to the washington post that  they've made to wired in january this  year firstly that they would not be  commenting on the allegations against  reginald until they'd concluded their  own internal investigation and secondly  a statement from reginald in which he  described his nature as intense  passionate and driven and that if he  feels someone is not delivering he  shares feedback bluntly and directly he  also said again that looking back his  vocabulary was too harsh at times and  that he knows he needs to work on his  delivery reginald replied to the article  in the tsm subreddit explaining that he  was not the direct manager of the head  of hr who was let go he said they had  disagreed on the proposal plan of  recruiting from another company in order  to build strong relationships with them  reginald disagreed saying the other  company was a competitor and that the  proposal showed a lack of prioritization  for these reasons he thought it would be  best to part ways sooner rather than  later the comment was down voted well  over a hundred times and many people in  the comments were calling reginald out  for not addressing the rest of the  article on wednesday doublelift reacted  to reginald's reddit comment on stream  and said that reginald had tried to sue  him for comments that he made last year  he's sitting there crying he's so  furious he's talking to stories like  what can i do man how  dude how can i get this guy to stop  talking about me yeah i still i still  have the letter of when he he threatened  to sue me for the first time dude it's  it's so insanely crazy it's it's like i  called him out for being a bully who  silences like the voices of his like  underlings and then he tries to threaten  to sue me  for disparaging his company the  following day doublelift shared the  letter he received from tsm lawyers a  few days after his stream in november  2021 it stated that the comments made by  doublelift then constituted multiple  material and incurable breaches of his  employment agreement with tsm they  claimed he shared confidential  information that breached both his  employment and release agreement and  that he went against both agreements to  not disparage or make defamatory and  unprofessional remarks against tsm or  any affiliates business structures  operations practices or management the  letter finished by stating that tsm  would be evaluating each breach and  exploring its legal options they listed  liquidated damages of one hundred  thousand dollars for each breach of the  employment agreement and two hundred  thousand dollars for each breach of the  release agreement doublelift had shared  the letter on stream the day before  releasing it on twitter and far from  being intimidated by it he felt it  helped his cause  let me just tell you guys that this  whole thing just completely plays into  the  uh idea that andy is a huge bully and  that he can get away with he wants  because he's powerful  it's so funny that it just like  completely proves my point doublelift  presented the papers as an attempt to  sue him i spoke to our in-house legal  counsel who said that these papers are a  cease-and-desist and contract  termination letter tsm state they are  evaluating the alleged breaches and  intend to pursue legal action i.e suing  to recover damages from doublelift  moving now from the legal world to the  court of public opinion things couldn't  get much worse for reginald right now  he's being slammed yet again within the  community after another scathing article  which alleges toxic bullying treatment  of his employees his attempt to explain  the initial accusation of the article in  tsm's own subreddit has been downvoted  and piled on by both tsm fans and the  wider community and to top it all off  doublelift has called him out again as  he has done at every step of this story  we still don't know when the findings of  riot's investigation will be published  but one thing is for sure when they are  it will be monumental if they find him  to be innocent or are seen to be being  too lenient with him they could be  accused of cowing to the influence that  tsm has as a major brand within the lcs  if they come down on him like a ton of  bricks i don't think it's an  exaggeration to say it could set a  precedent for the north american scene  the wider league scene in general and  perhaps even esports the world over so  we await the report and if anything  happens before then we'll be sure to let  you know  you

